# TraeCN MCP

TraeCN MCP is a local-first stdio server for operating the TraeCN desktop app.
MCP contract version 5 exposes exactly 20 tools for tasks, workspace, model,
mode, conversations, settings, and exceptional decisions. One local gateway
owns execution, queues, persistence, and completion delivery.

## Quick start

Requires macOS, Node.js 22+, and a signed-in TraeCN desktop app.

```sh
npm install --global https://github.com/Luckycat133/traecn-mcp/releases/download/v{{VERSION}}/traecnclaw-{{VERSION}}.tgz
traecn-mcp quickstart --launch-trae
```

Keep the gateway terminal open. Quickstart prints recovery instructions if
TraeCN is already open without remote debugging.

In another terminal, run `traecn-mcp setup-mcp`. Add the generated `traecn`
entry to your MCP host and reconnect. Call `traecn_send_message` and keep the
returned task ID for completion notifications or a `traecn_get_task` read.

The web console at [127.0.0.1:8788](http://127.0.0.1:8788/) offers human control
and task review on the same gateway.

## Other install options

The [matching release](https://github.com/Luckycat133/traecn-mcp/releases/tag/v{{VERSION}})
contains the server tarball and MCPB bundle. Homebrew installs the same server:

```sh
brew tap Luckycat133/traecn-mcp https://github.com/Luckycat133/traecn-mcp.git
brew install Luckycat133/traecn-mcp/traecnclaw
```

Hosts that support Agent Skills can also install the tool-use guidance:

```sh
npx skills add https://github.com/Luckycat133/traecn-mcp --skill traecn-mcp -g
```

## Runtime

The server and gateway run beside TraeCN on your Mac. The gateway defaults to
`127.0.0.1:8788`; configure authentication before a non-loopback bind. Directory
builds can inspect the stdio schema.

The server supports MCP `2026-07-28` with optional Tasks negotiation, plus
initialization-based `2025-11-25` and `2024-11-05` clients.

